        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kuala Lumpur, KLCC vicinity\n- Buildings: KLCC District Cooling, Petronas Twin Towers, Suria KLCC, Maxis Tower, Menara Exxon Mobil, Kuala Lumpur Convention Centre, Mandarin Oriental Kuala Lumpur, As Syakirin Mosque\n- Systems: district cooling, chilled water unit\n\nFacts:\n- KLCC District Cooling is a building used to provide district cooling for the KLCC vicinity in Kuala Lumpur.\n- KLCC District Cooling has a 30,000-ton gas-powered turbine-driven chilled water unit.\n- The chilled water unit at KLCC District Cooling provides cooling to the Petronas Twin Towers, Suria KLCC, Maxis Tower, Menara Exxon Mobil, Kuala Lumpur Convention Centre, Mandarin Oriental Kuala Lumpur, and As Syakirin Mosque.\n- Suria KLCC is a shopping centre located in central Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia.",
